acintosh-style computer with an equally blank screen sits a little farther back. The black cube is the focal object, evoking the acquisition that brought core software and Jobs back, not suggesting that hardware parts were physically fused. A pair of adult hands gently sets the cube on the desk; no celebrity portrait is necessary. Soft window daylight, muted sage shelving and warm ivory space. No company marks, operating-system lettering, money, timelines or charts.",
